  "$comment": "What each contract operation needs from the user's GUI Access Group (§1, §11). Product owner 2026-10-25 (backend step 10): every call is checked on the server, reads too: a read needs the page's View, a change the action. A page the user may not open is not reached from another page either; other pages pick its records by name through /lookups (lookups: which pages may use each kind). Admin pages (admin) are for administrators only, unless the user's access group (or the user's own override) names that page itself; the group's Every page grant never covers them. An operation's page comes from its path's first segment (segments) unless operations names it; its action comes from its method and operationId (scripts/generate.mjs) unless operations names it. open: no check beyond being signed in (the user's own session, preferences, saved views, own undo; the portal has its own sign-in). An action the page does not offer (pages: each page's actions, kept equal to the Admin › Access Groups catalogue by mock/test/access.test.ts) falls back to edit, else view. contract/generated/operations.json is the result.",
